    "category": "Top-Freezer, 18 cu. ft.",
    "badge": "Best Low-Risk Pick",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Top-freezer layout has the fewest moving parts of any common refrigerator design",
      "Simple controls and no through-the-door dispenser to fail",
      "Whirlpool parts and technicians are widely available across the country",
      "Sized for apartments, rentals and small households at 18 cubic feet",
      "Typically one of the more affordable ways to buy from a major brand"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Fresh food sits low, so you bend more than with a French door",
      "No ice-and-water dispenser in the door"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The default recommendation for anyone who wants a dependable refrigerator without paying for features. Whirlpool and a top-freezer layout is the conservative choice that rarely disappoints.",
