    ],
    "bottomLine": "A sensible mid-priced choice when door swing space is limited and you want ice and water on demand.",
    "description": "Side-by-side refrigerators solve a specific problem: tight kitchens where two wide French doors would collide with an island or a wall. This GE model is a long-running example of the layout, with a tall freezer on one side, a tall fresh-food section on the other and a dispenser on the door. For households that use a lot of ice and filtered water, the dispenser is the main attraction, and the full-height freezer is easier to scan than a pull-out drawer. The downsides are structural. Wide items do not fit flat, and freezer space can feel stacked rather than open. GE is owned by Haier and sells through a large dealer and technician network, which helps when something needs service. As with any dispenser model, install a proper supply line and replace the filter on schedule to protect the valve and tubing."
  },
  {
    "id": "samsung-rf28t5001sr",
    "name": "Samsung 28 cu. ft. 3-Door French Door Refrigerator (RF28T5001SR)",
    "category": "French Door, Standard Depth",
    "badge": "Best Capacity per Dollar",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Roughly 28 cubic feet of capacity gives families plenty of fresh and frozen space",
      "French door layout puts everyday food at eye level with wide shelves",
      "Samsung has advertised extended coverage on its inverter compressor",
      "Typically priced below premium French door models with similar capacity",
      "Large freezer drawer is deep enough for bulk shopping"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Standard depth sticks out beyond kitchen counters",
      "Samsung ice-maker designs are a frequent topic in owner forums"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The best pick when your priority is the most storage for the money and you do not need a flush look.",
    "description": "Samsung built its refrigerator business on large-capacity French door models, and this one is a representative family-sized example. The wide fresh-food shelves hold platters and sheet pans, and the bottom freezer drawer gives better access than a side-by-side for bulk frozen food. Because the cabinet is standard depth, it holds more than a counter-depth model of the same width, though it extends past your counters. The brand markets a digital inverter compressor with extended coverage; read the current terms for this exact model, because the warranty typically covers the compressor and not every part. Owners commonly discuss ice-maker reliability on this style of refrigerator across brands, so weigh whether you will use the ice maker daily. If you will not, a model without one or a separate countertop unit can reduce risk."
  },
  {
    "id": "lg-lrmvc2306s",
    "name": "LG 23 cu. ft. Counter-Depth MAX 4-Door French Door (LRMVC2306S)",
    "category": "Counter-Depth French Door, 4-Door",
    "badge": "Best Counter-Depth Features",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Counter-depth cabinet sits close to flush with standard counters",
      "Four-door layout adds a convertible middle drawer for flexible storage",
      "LG has advertised extended coverage on its linear compressor",
      "Wide fresh-food shelves hold large trays despite the shallow cabinet",
      "Smart features available for those who want them"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Counter-depth designs hold less food than standard-depth refrigerators of the same width",
      "More compartments mean more seals and more parts to service"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A feature-rich way to get a built-in look without a premium-brand price tag. Worth it if you will use the extra drawer.",
    "description": "LG leans into the counter-depth category with models that aim to look like a built-in without custom cabinetry. This four-door model keeps the French door layout and adds a convertible middle drawer, which can hold deli items and party platters or run as extra freezer space. The shallow cabinet delivers the flush look, though doors and handles still protrude beyond the counter line. LG markets a linear compressor and has advertised an extended compressor warranty; as with any brand, check the current terms for the specific model. The trade-off is capacity: 23 cubic feet in a counter-depth body is not the same as 23 cubic feet in a standard cabinet, so compare the interior dimensions with your shopping habits. For households that cook for guests, the flexible drawer is the highlight."
  },
  {
    "id": "bosch-b36cd50sns",
    "name": "Bosch 500 Series 36-inch Counter-Depth French Door (B36CD50SNS)",
    "category": "Counter-Depth French Door, Design-Led",
    "badge": "Best for Design-Led Kitchens",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Slim counter-depth cabinet with a clean European-influenced look",
      "Fits 36-inch openings common in new construction and renovations",
      "Bosch positions its refrigerators as quiet and understated",
      "Bottom-mount freezer drawer keeps frequently used food at eye level",
      "Pairs visually with other Bosch kitchen appliances"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Higher price than comparable Samsung or LG models",
      "Fewer smart features than Korean competitors"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "Buy this when the kitchen design drives the decision and you are willing to pay for a restrained, flush look over the longest feature list.",
    "description": "Bosch approaches refrigerators the way it approaches dishwashers: restrained styling, a focus on fit and finish, and fewer headline gimmicks than the Korean brands. This 500 Series counter-depth French door is sized for a 36-inch opening, which is the standard width in many renovated kitchens, and its shallow cabinet lines up closely with counters. Owners who choose this brand typically do so for the look and for the way it sits alongside other Bosch appliances. The cost is that you pay more per cubic foot than for Samsung or LG, and the smart features are more modest. Confirm the exact panel finish, handle style and any retailer-specific packages, as Bosch sells several close variants. If you prize quiet operation and a built-in appearance over capacity per dollar, this is the model to shortlist."
  },
  {
    "id": "kitchenaid-krfc302ess",
    "name": "KitchenAid 22 cu. ft. 36-inch Counter-Depth French Door (KRFC302ESS)",
    "category": "Counter-Depth French Door, Premium Finish",
    "badge": "Best Premium Brand Pick",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "KitchenAid sits in the Whirlpool Corporation family, with a broad parts network",
      "Counter-depth 36-inch cabinet for a near built-in appearance",
      "Premium finish and hardware that match KitchenAid ranges and dishwashers",
      "French door layout with wide shelves and a bottom freezer drawer",
      "Strong match for kitchens already using KitchenAid appliances"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Premium price for a capacity that is modest for its footprint",
      "Features overlap heavily with less expensive Whirlpool-family models"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A premium-brand counter-depth refrigerator that gives you a coordinated kitchen and access to a large service network.",
    "description": "KitchenAid is the premium brand of Whirlpool Corporation, and its refrigerators trade on finish quality and coordination with KitchenAid ranges and dishwashers. This 36-inch counter-depth French door model offers the flush look many buyers want, with a bottom-mount freezer drawer and wide fresh-food shelves. Because it shares a parent company with Whirlpool and Maytag, parts and service coverage are generally broad, which is a quiet advantage over some design-led alternatives. The honest caveat is value: you pay a premium for the badge and finish, and the cubic footage is modest for the size. Compare it with a Whirlpool or Maytag counter-depth model from the same family if your goal is simply a flush look. Choose the KitchenAid when finish, hardware and a matching suite of appliances are part of the brief."
  }
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 1,
          name: "Home",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 2,
          name: "Best Lists",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/best-of/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Best Refrigerator Brands",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/best-refrigerator-brands/",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which refrigerator brand is the most reliable?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No brand is reliable across every model, and published rankings vary by source and year. Simpler layouts such as top-freezers generally have fewer failure points. Rather than choosing by brand, shortlist models, read owner reviews for that exact unit, and check local repair availability."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Samsung or LG better for refrigerators?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Both brands make feature-rich French door models with inverter or linear compressors and extended compressor warranties. Neither is clearly superior. Compare the specific model, the ice-maker design, the warranty terms and the price, and use owner reviews for the exact model number you are considering."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long should a refrigerator last?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Manufacturers and appliance trade sources commonly cite roughly a decade or more for a well-maintained refrigerator, though lifespan varies with model, usage and conditions. Cleaning the condenser coils, replacing water filters and keeping door gaskets intact all help extend its service life."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a counter-depth refrigerator worth it?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It is worth it if the flush look matters to you and you can accept less capacity for the same width. A counter-depth model sits closer to your counters but holds less food. If storage matters more than appearance, a standard-depth cabinet is better value."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Should I buy a refrigerator with an ice maker?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Only if you will use it regularly. Ice makers and dispensers are among the most commonly serviced components. If you rarely use ice, a model without one, or a separate countertop ice maker, reduces the number of parts that can fail in the main refrigerator."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What temperature should a refrigerator be set to?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Food safety guidance generally recommends keeping the fresh-food compartment at or below 40°F and the freezer at 0°F. Use a standalone thermometer rather than trusting the dial, and allow a full day for a new unit to stabilise before judging."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "When is the best time to buy a refrigerator?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Retailers commonly discount appliances around holiday weekends such as Memorial Day, Labor Day and Black Friday, and clear older models as new ones arrive. Compare against recent prices, and make sure the model fits your space and water line before chasing a deal."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "The Honest Reviewers" },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: authorName(Astro.url.pathname),
    section: "Home Appliances",
    tags: [
      "best refrigerator brands",
      "best refrigerators",
      "refrigerator brands compared",
      "French door refrigerator",
      "counter-depth refrigerator",
      "top freezer refrigerator"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Brand-by-Brand Guide
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Best Refrigerator <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">Brands in 2026</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          A refrigerator runs for a decade or more, so the brand matters less than the layout, the compressor and the service network behind it. Here are seven models that make the case for their makers.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#whirlpool-wrt318fzdw"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#top-picks"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            Compare All 7 Models
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Shaheer Ali Khan</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">Consumer Product Testing &amp; Materials Performance Specialist</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="14.9k" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#short-answer" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. The Short Answer</a>
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. Our 7 Top Picks Reviewed</a>
          <a href="#brand-families" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. Who Owns Which Brand</a>
          <a href="#layouts" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. Layouts: Top-Freezer to French Door</a>
          <a href="#compressors" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. Compressors and Energy Use</a>
          <a href="#sizing" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Sizing and Counter-Depth</a>
          <a href="#ice-water" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. Ice Makers and Water Lines</a>
          <a href="#warranty" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Warranty and Service</a>
          <a href="#timing" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. When to Buy</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">11. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Every refrigerator brand makes a good model and a disappointing one, and the badge on the door predicts less than the shopping lists suggest. What predicts satisfaction is matching the layout to your kitchen, understanding the ice maker you are signing up for, and knowing who will repair it. This guide ranks seven real models from seven brands, and explains what each brand family is genuinely good at.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. The Short Answer: Which Brand for Which Kitchen
          </h2>

          <p>
            If you want one sentence, here it is: buy the layout first and the brand second. A basic top-freezer from Whirlpool or Frigidaire is the lowest-risk purchase in the category, a French door from LG or Samsung gives you the most features per dollar, and a counter-depth model from Bosch or KitchenAid is what you buy when the kitchen design drives the decision. GE sits in the middle with a broad range and one of the largest service networks in the country.
          </p>

          <p>
            Brand reputations in this category are built on two things that have nothing to do with how cold the food stays. The first is how often a model's ice maker, water dispenser or electronic control board fails, which owners and appliance technicians discuss constantly. The second is how easy it is to get a repair person and a replacement part. A brand with a slightly lower feature count and a deep service network can be the better ownership experience.
          </p>

          <p>
            We deliberately avoid declaring a single winner by brand. Reliability numbers published by retailers and surveys change year to year, vary by model line, and are rarely comparable across sources, so treating any one ranking as settled would be overselling it. What we can do is tell you what each brand family is known for, which models we would shortlist, and which mistakes cost buyers the most.
          </p>

          <p>
            Start with the table below, then read the picks. If you are replacing a refrigerator that died suddenly, skim the section on <a href="/what-temperature-should-a-refrigerator-be/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold hover:underline">what temperature a refrigerator should hold</a> before you throw out any food, and make sure your delivery date does not leave you without cold storage.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Brand</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Model shown</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Layout</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Best for</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Whirlpool</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">WRT318FZDW</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Top-freezer</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Simple, lower-risk purchase</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Frigidaire</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">FFHT1835VS</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Top-freezer</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Budget and rental kitchens</td>
                  </tr>
