          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            10. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying on brand reputation alone</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A brand's good name rarely applies equally to every model it sells. Compare the specific model number, read owner reviews for that exact unit, and weigh layout and ice-maker complexity at least as heavily as the badge on the door.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring the delivery path</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Many refrigerators never make it into the kitchen on the first attempt because a doorway, stairwell or hallway turn is too tight. Measure every point from the street to the final location, including door swing and handle clearance.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying for features you will not use</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Smart screens, flex drawers and in-door ice systems add parts that can fail. If you will not use them weekly, a simpler layout is cheaper to buy, cheaper to repair and often lasts longer without a service call.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Skipping the water line preparation</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Ice-maker models need a shut-off valve and a proper supply line. Cheap plastic tubing can kink or leak behind the unit. Use a braided line, leave slack, and check the fitting a day after installation for slow drips.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming counter-depth means the same capacity</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A counter-depth cabinet holds less than a standard-depth cabinet of the same width. Compare interior dimensions and stated cubic footage, and be realistic about how much food you store before choosing a shallow design.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

