        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Which refrigerator brand is the most reliable?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                No brand is reliable across every model, and published rankings vary by source and year. Simpler layouts such as top-freezers generally have fewer failure points. Rather than choosing by brand, shortlist models, read owner reviews for that exact unit, and check local repair availability.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is Samsung or LG better for refrigerators?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Both brands make feature-rich French door models with inverter or linear compressors and extended compressor warranties. Neither is clearly superior. Compare the specific model, the ice-maker design, the warranty terms and the price, and use owner reviews for the exact model number you are considering.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How long should a refrigerator last?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Manufacturers and appliance trade sources commonly cite roughly a decade or more for a well-maintained refrigerator, though lifespan varies with model, usage and conditions. Cleaning the condenser coils, replacing water filters and keeping door gaskets intact all help extend its service life.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is a counter-depth refrigerator worth it?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It is worth it if the flush look matters to you and you can accept less capacity for the same width. A counter-depth model sits closer to your counters but holds less food. If storage matters more than appearance, a standard-depth cabinet is better value.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Should I buy a refrigerator with an ice maker?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Only if you will use it regularly. Ice makers and dispensers are among the most commonly serviced components. If you rarely use ice, a model without one, or a separate countertop ice maker, reduces the number of parts that can fail in the main refrigerator.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What temperature should a refrigerator be set to?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Food safety guidance generally recommends keeping the fresh-food compartment at or below 40°F and the freezer at 0°F. Use a standalone thermometer rather than trusting the dial, and allow a full day for a new unit to stabilise before judging.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">When is the best time to buy a refrigerator?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Retailers commonly discount appliances around holiday weekends such as Memorial Day, Labor Day and Black Friday, and clear older models as new ones arrive. Compare against recent prices, and make sure the model fits your space and water line before chasing a deal.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>

